---
// /blog/late-night-food/ — AGENTS.md-bound slug (v1 URL stub points here).
//
// Phase 4 honesty fix: v1's version of this post promised "late-night
// availability" and "fresh food, even at night", while site.config.json says
// the kitchen closes at 21:00. Search engines and customers both punish that
// kind of contradiction, so the post now targets the same query truthfully —
// the craving is real, the closing time is 9 PM, here is how to plan around it.
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import BlogPostLayout from '../../components/BlogPostLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../lib/data';
import { LINKS, abs, blogPostingJsonLd, breadcrumbJsonLd } from '../../lib/seo';

const headline = 'Late-Night Food in Sundargarh: Order Before 9 PM';
const description =
  'Options thin out fast after 9 PM in Sundargarh. How to plan a late dinner, what to order so it still tastes good an hour later, and when we close.';
const image = {
  url: abs('/static/images/blog_images/blog_3.webp'),
  width: 1024,
  height: 1024,
  alt: 'Late-night pure veg food in Sundargarh',
};
const path = '/blog/late-night-food/';
---

<Layout
  title={headline}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  image={image}
  jsonLd={[
    blogPostingJsonLd({
      headline,
      description,
      path,
      image: image.url,
      datePublished: '2024-05-25',
    }),
    breadcrumbJsonLd([
      { name: 'Blog', path: '/blog/' },
      { name: 'Late-Night Food', path },
    ]),
  ]}
>
  <BlogPostLayout
    line1="LATE-NIGHT"
    lineGradient="FOOD."
    subtitle="How to eat well late in Sundargarh — and when to place the order."
  >
    <p class="subtitle" style="font-weight: 600; color: #555; margin-top: -10px">
      Raat ke time kya order karein?
    </p>

    <picture>
      <source type="image/avif" srcset="/static/images/blog_images/blog_3.avif" />
      <source type="image/webp" srcset="/static/images/blog_images/blog_3.webp" />
      <img
        src="/static/images/blog_images/blog_3.webp"
        alt="Late-night pure veg food in Sundargarh"
        class="blog-img"
        loading="lazy"
        width="1024"
        height="1024"
        style="background: #eee"
      />
    </picture>

    <p>
      Anyone who has been hungry in Sundargarh at half past nine knows the problem: the hunger is at
      full strength and the options are not. Shutters are down, kitchens are cleaned, and whatever is
      still open is not what you actually wanted.
    </p>

    <h3>First, the honest part about our timings</h3>
    <p>
      The Oven Vibe is open {site.business.hours.display}. We are not a 2 AM kitchen, and we would
      rather say so than take an order we cannot cook well. If you want a proper late dinner from us,
      the trick is to order before the craving peaks — place it by about 8:30 PM and you are
      comfortably inside the window.
    </p>

    <h3>Who orders late, and why planning helps</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Hostel students and bachelors, after study or a shift</li>
      <li>Night-shift workers eating before or after work</li>
      <li>Movie nights and gaming sessions that run long</li>
      <li>Anyone who skipped a proper dinner and regretted it at 9 PM</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>What to order for later, not just for now</h3>
    <p>
      Not everything survives an hour on a table. These hold up best if you will be eating a while
      after it arrives:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Pizzas</strong> — reheat well in a pan, and the paneer ones stay soft instead of going
        rubbery.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Fried rice bowls</strong> — the most forgiving thing on the menu, and filling enough to
        be an actual dinner.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Fries and potato pops</strong> — best eaten immediately, so order these only if you are
        eating straight away.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Meal box combos</strong> — one box, nothing to assemble, ideal when you cannot be
        bothered to think about it.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="highlight-box">
      <h3>Ordering late, done right</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Call or message by 8:30 PM for a comfortable evening delivery.</li>
        <li>
          A group order past ₹{site.delivery.free_above} pays no delivery charge, which is usually the
          cheapest way to feed four people.
        </li>
        <li>Collecting yourself? Takeaway is ready in about 20 minutes.</li>
      </ul>
      <p style="margin-top: 10px; font-weight: 700; color: #ad210a">
        Everything is 100% pure veg — no exceptions, at any hour.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h3>The last bite</h3>
    <p>
      Late hunger is easier to solve with five minutes of planning than with a search at 10 PM. Keep
      the <a href="/menu/">menu</a> handy,
      know <a href="/sundargarh/">the delivery charge for your area</a>, and put the order in before the
      kitchen closes.
    </p>

    <a href={`tel:${site.business.phone}`} class="cta">
      Call the Kitchen: {site.business.phone_display}
    </a>
    <p>
      Prefer to type? <a href={LINKS.whatsapp} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >Order on WhatsApp</a
      >.
    </p>
  </BlogPostLayout>
</Layout>
